The feature is enabled only by the new flag. It captures at most 131,072
entry summaries, each with requested cycles, entry TSC, CR3/RBP/RSP and up to
four caller links read through the existing RAM-only diagnostic walk. The
matching debug ELF has BuildID
`338e542e384c46228f7a378babc0f9bb2b6a5997` and SHA-256
`7e460f048c3de0f8ee85fd326f2f65d95a6ee448e57b6f5333e2be79b5be9d1f`.
Disassembly shows `delay_tsc` pushes RBP and establishes its frame before the
entry RDTSC at `+0x1b`. Thus the first stored return link is
`__const_udelay+0x3d`; the next link is the caller of `__const_udelay`.

