Per-caller and requested-cycle attribution
------------------------------------------
Calls are grouped by the next frame above the common `__const_udelay+0x3d`
return site and by the captured `R8` requested-cycle value. Return addresses
were resolved against the matching debug ELF:

| Caller | Request | Run 0001 calls / polls | Run 0002 calls / polls | Delta calls / polls |
|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|
| `vpanic+0x497` (`0xffffffff81214ae7`) | `0xf4217` | 33,894 / 33,043,619 | 33,905 / 33,054,194 | **+11 / +10,575** |
| `mc146818_avoid_UIP+0xfb` (`0xffffffff822e5dab`) | `0x1869c` | 10,000 / 989,998 | 10,000 / 989,998 | 0 / 0 |
| `init_8259A` | mixed, mostly `0x7d0` | 9 / 114 | 9 / 114 | 0 / 0 |
| `__udelay+0x15` | mixed | 10 / 3,971 | 10 / 3,798 | 0 / -173 |
| `serial8250_THRE_test` | `0x3e8` | 2 / 2 | 2 / 2 | 0 / 0 |
| **Total** |  | **43,915 / 34,037,704** | **43,926 / 34,048,106** | **+11 / +10,402** |

The run-length encodings of the 23 caller/request blocks have the same block
order in both runs. The vpanic block has median 975 polls per call in both
runs; its means are 974.9106 and 974.9062. Its one terminal partial call is
938 polls in run 0001 and 787 in run 0002. Since the vpanic block contains
tens of thousands of identical caller/request keys, individual calls are not
forced into ordinal pairs. Its poll-count distribution remains concentrated
at 975; the +11 calls account for most of the +10,575 block poll increase.
The other caller blocks contribute -173 polls, which reconciles the total
+10,402 poll difference. The entry histogram delta is entirely in the vpanic
block.

Conclusion and limits
---------------------
The per-call summaries explain where the differing reads accumulated: run 2
made 11 additional `delay_tsc` calls from `vpanic+0x497` through
`__const_udelay`, and that block accounts for +10,575 polls. Rare
initialization/`__udelay` calls contribute -173 polls; `mc146818_avoid_UIP`
is unchanged. This is caller-level localization, not proof why vpanic issued
the extra calls or whether they were caused by the nonce. It does not explain
the separate +1 page fault, establish UART-difference benignity, or satisfy
S5-07 acceptance. The source series' strict comparator remains
`matches=false` on machine observations and nonce-normalized UART; no
comparator or allowlist changes were made.
